cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  An enzyme-resolved dataset linking drug interaction mechanisms to
  clinical severity grades
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Noor
    given-names: Adeeb
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8251-1853"
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Information Technology, Faculty of Computing and
      Information Technology, King Abdulaziz University, Jeddah, Saudi Arabia
    email: arnoor@kau.edu.sa
abstract: >-
  A harmonised, enzyme-resolved drug-drug interaction resource that joins a
  mechanistic DDI corpus (GoldD3R, D3-derived, UMLS CUI-indexed) to a
  severity-graded clinical corpus (DDInter 2.0) and attributes each
  interaction to the specific cytochrome P450 enzyme or membrane transporter
  responsible for it. Contains 1,900 enzyme-annotated drug pairs spanning 240
  drugs and 35 enzymes and transporters, per-enzyme association statistics
  with FDR control and E-values, enzyme-phenotype enrichment signatures, and
  four independent external validations (DrugBank hard-proven set, curated
  KEGG DDI set, clinical-trial adverse-event reports, trueDDI gold set). A
  self-contained interactive browser is included.
keywords:
  - drug-drug interactions
  - pharmacokinetics
  - cytochrome P450
  - drug transporters
  - DDInter
  - DrugBank
  - KEGG
  - pharmacovigilance
  - data harmonisation
